# Analyses are excluded from linting, deliberately.
#
# sqlfluff's duckdb dialect cannot parse GROUPING SETS, which the 1a queries use
# for the per-brand quarter subtotal and grand total. It is valid DuckDB and runs
# correctly; the parser gap then cascades into spurious layout and reference
# violations in the same file.
#
# The layout rules in ../.sqlfluff are also tuned for models -- positional
# GROUP BY / ORDER BY reads well in a model with a fixed column list, but these
# analyses end in `select *` where `order by 10 desc, 7 asc` would be far less
# readable than naming the columns.
#
# Correctness is verified by execution instead: both 1a versions return identical
# 25-row results and both 1b versions are byte-identical. See
# data_quality_register.md.
*.sql
